  <h1>About TableScore</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>TableScore is a working title for a small static site that keeps score while people play physical cards. Version 0.2 ships one complete tool: a <a href="/hand-and-foot-score-keeper/">Hand and Foot score keeper</a>.</p>
    <p>It does not deal cards, play the hand, or connect players across devices. You tap what happened at the table — piles, red threes, card counts, who went out — and the scoring engine applies the selected published variant.</p>
    <p>Scores are stored only in this browser (localStorage). There are no accounts. There is no live advertising network in this sandbox; the empty boxes on the game page are reserved height only.</p>
    <p>TableScore is not affiliated with Bicycle, the United States Playing Card Company, any canasta publisher, or John McLeod / Pagat. The Hand and Foot explainer cites Pagat as a public rules source. It does not reproduce a full rulebook.</p>
    <p>This site is a social score pad. It is not a place to play for money.</p>
    <p><a href="/hand-and-foot-score-keeper/">Open the Hand and Foot tool</a> · <a href="/hand-and-foot-score-sheet.pdf" download="hand-and-foot-score-sheet.pdf">Download the PDF score sheet</a> · <a href="/printable/hand-and-foot-score-sheet/">Print a paper sheet</a> · <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> · <a href="/contact/">Contact</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>
